cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. It is a research and
  education project that works on synthetic data and is not validated for any clinical
  use.
type: software
title: oncogenomics-biomarker-workbench
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research and education workbench for exploring synthetic
  transcriptomics-style data: data validation, quality control, a transparent two-group
  comparison (Welch t-test, Cohen's d, Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment), documented
  ranking, figures, reports, and a local Streamlit dashboard. It is not a medical device
  and makes no clinical or biomarker claims.
authors:
  - family-names: Copeland
    given-names: Jonathan
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JonathanMCopelandJr/oncogenomics-biomarker-workbench"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - education
  - reproducible research
  - synthetic data
  - transcriptomics
  - streamlit
